4	/**
5	 * Dunning windows, all measured in DAYS PAST EXPIRY — the SINGLE resolver for
6	 * Settings → Billing's three fields (grace / warn / terminate) plus the
7	 * "Auto-suspend overdue accounts" kill switch.
8	 *
9	 * MOVED HERE FROM worker/billing.ts (2026-09-25), verbatim, so a second real
10	 * caller — the admin server fleet list's "Deleting soon" tag — can compute
11	 * exactly how close a SUSPENDED-unpaid server is to the real termination the
12	 * sweep will perform, instead of a second copy of this clamp math that could
13	 * silently disagree with what actually deletes a server. `worker/billing.ts`
14	 * now imports `dunningConfig` from here rather than defining its own; nothing
15	 * about its behavior changed, only where the function lives.
16	 *
17	 * The legacy env vars remain as fallbacks, converted onto the days-past-expiry
18	 * clock so an operator who had set them keeps the behaviour they configured
19	 * (NXEON_TERMINATE_DAYS counted forward from the END of grace, and
20	 * NXEON_WARN_BEFORE_TERMINATE_DAYS counted backwards from termination).
21	 *
22	 * `CARD_SUSPEND_DAY`/`SUSPEND_SLIP_CAP_DAYS` are imported from
23	 * lib/dunning-schedule.ts (itself guarded by test/payment-method-ui.test.ts to
24	 * match worker/billing.ts's own constants exactly), rather than re-declared a
25	 * third time.
26	 */
27	export type DunningConfig = {
28	  /** Days past expiry before an account with no card in play is suspended. */
29	  graceDays: number;
30	  /** Days past expiry when the "will be deleted" warning goes out. */
31	  warnDays: number;
32	  /** Days past expiry when an unpaid SUSPENDED server is destroyed. */
33	  terminateDays: number;
34	  /** Admin kill switch: when false the sweep suspends and terminates nothing. */
35	  autoSuspend: boolean;
36	};
